WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.270
Keep on holding me

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.270
Daite ite mune de anata no koe wo kiite iru

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:09.150
I listen to your voice in your arms

00:00:04.270 --> 00:00:09.150
Daite ite mune de anata no koe wo kiite iru

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:21.960
If I reach out in the light, I can touch

00:00:10.820 --> 00:00:21.960
Hikari no naka ni te wo sashinobaseba todoku

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.130
The precious arms

00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:27.130
Anna ni motomete ita kakegae no nai ude e

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:32.130
I have been searching for so hard

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:32.130
Anna ni motomete ita kakegae no nai ude e

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:39.470
I turn around and the sky of blue

00:00:33.010 --> 00:00:39.470
Furimukeba kodoku ni wa

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:48.940
Smiles down upon my solitude

00:00:40.310 --> 00:00:48.940
Sora ga aoku hohoende kureru

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:56.200
In the darkness, I nearly lose sight of my dreams

00:00:49.150 --> 00:00:56.200
Kurayami ni yume wo miushinai sou ni naru

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:04.120
But if you remain by my side

00:00:56.740 --> 00:01:04.120
Demo anata ga itekureru no nara

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.420
Keep on holding me

00:01:04.660 --> 00:01:08.420
Daite ite mune de anata no koe wo kiite iru

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.090
I listen to your voice in your arms

00:01:08.420 --> 00:01:12.090
Daite ite mune de anata no koe wo kiite iru

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:19.260
I want to protect this love for always

00:01:12.090 --> 00:01:19.260
Itsudemo kono omoi wo mamoritai no

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:24.600
This love...

00:01:19.510 --> 00:01:24.600
Omoi wo

00:02:46.430 --> 00:02:49.940
Something That Must Be Protected

00:02:51.350 --> 00:02:54.190
Kurau... Where are we going from here?

00:02:54.820 --> 00:02:55.820
Earth...

00:02:56.480 --> 00:03:00.200
The first place I lived
after being separated from Dad.

00:03:00.740 --> 00:03:01.660
We'll go there.

00:03:02.070 --> 00:03:04.280
A place where the GPO won't come?

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:08.160
Yes, a peaceful place they don't know about.

00:03:09.250 --> 00:03:12.170
A place that's precious to Dad and me.

00:03:12.750 --> 00:03:17.460
But it looks like we can't board the shuttle
because the GPO has set up security checks.

00:03:17.920 --> 00:03:19.720
What are we going to do, Kurau?

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:22.180
What should we do...

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:24.390
Dad...

00:03:37.400 --> 00:03:39.110
I'm glad I saw you again.

00:03:39.110 --> 00:03:41.860
I will do what I must do.

00:03:42.410 --> 00:03:46.450
So you... You two... must live in this world.

00:03:46.910 --> 00:03:49.250
No matter what happens, you must live!

00:03:49.250 --> 00:03:50.000
Dad!

00:03:53.960 --> 00:03:55.630
No matter what...

00:03:56.840 --> 00:03:58.670
What do you want?!

00:03:58.670 --> 00:04:00.210
Let me see your ID card.

00:04:00.210 --> 00:04:01.880
I don't have it with me right now.

00:04:01.880 --> 00:04:03.010
Let go of me!

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.720
Did I do something wrong?

00:04:04.720 --> 00:04:07.470
All transportation facilities
are under heavy security right now.

00:04:07.470 --> 00:04:09.970
I'm just gonna go see my friend.

00:04:09.970 --> 00:04:12.520
Got a problem with that? Let go of me, old man!

00:04:12.520 --> 00:04:14.520
If you keep fighting us, then...

00:04:14.520 --> 00:04:17.820
Then don't touch me. I hate being touched!

00:04:17.820 --> 00:04:20.110
We're going to have to take you down to the station.

00:04:30.540 --> 00:04:35.290
Hey, you over there at Gate 3! Ship number XR-24!

00:04:35.290 --> 00:04:37.040
What are you doing, cutting in line?!

00:04:37.040 --> 00:04:38.880
It's not your turn yet.

00:04:38.880 --> 00:04:41.090
Keep to your departure time, will ya?

00:04:41.090 --> 00:04:44.220
Come on, gimme a break and do me a favor again.

00:04:44.220 --> 00:04:47.640
I'm running late and the other party's getting upset.

00:04:47.640 --> 00:04:51.680
Jeez, I tell you... But this is the last time, all right?

00:04:51.680 --> 00:04:52.810
Thanks a lot.

00:05:02.320 --> 00:05:03.490
It went well.

00:05:05.070 --> 00:05:06.950
Thank you, Jose.

00:05:06.950 --> 00:05:11.410
Now we're even... I mean, I can repay you
for the favor you did for me.

00:05:11.240 --> 00:05:15.250
Protection 
from evil 
on the Moon

00:05:12.250 --> 00:05:13.790
Are you sure this was okay?

00:05:13.790 --> 00:05:15.250
Don't worry about it.

00:05:15.580 --> 00:05:18.330
You saved Jose's life.

00:05:18.790 --> 00:05:23.050
You're an important guest on this ship.
Relax, you're in good hands.

00:05:23.050 --> 00:05:25.970
Although actually, it's just a second-hand ship.

00:05:25.970 --> 00:05:28.430
You'd better not be making fun of my precious ship!

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:30.100
I'm just kidding!

00:05:30.100 --> 00:05:32.850
Man, you're so childish!

00:05:35.890 --> 00:05:39.770
I can't thank you enough.

00:05:40.400 --> 00:05:43.070
Not only did you save my life,

00:05:43.610 --> 00:05:46.650
but you let me see my wife and kids again.

00:05:47.490 --> 00:05:52.200
Without you, I would've caused
my family a lot of pain.

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:56.330
My daughter calls you an angel, you know.

00:05:57.210 --> 00:05:58.080
Me?

00:05:58.370 --> 00:05:59.080
Yeah.

00:06:09.930 --> 00:06:13.310
There's no sign of them boarding any shuttle.

00:06:14.310 --> 00:06:18.850
Maybe they realized that it was impossible
to evade such heavy security...

00:06:18.850 --> 00:06:22.320
Don't jump to conclusions.
That's a bad habit of yours.

00:06:22.320 --> 00:06:23.190
I'm sorry.

00:06:24.730 --> 00:06:25.610
Could this be it?

00:06:25.610 --> 00:06:26.240
What?

00:06:26.650 --> 00:06:29.910
There's one ship that took off
at an unscheduled time.

00:06:29.910 --> 00:06:30.950
That must be it!

00:06:32.490 --> 00:06:33.620
A freighter?

00:06:34.660 --> 00:06:36.790
It left six hours ahead of schedule.

00:06:36.790 --> 00:06:38.830
Someone must be helping Kurau.

00:06:39.210 --> 00:06:43.540
Form a pursuit team, seize this ship and capture those two.

00:06:43.540 --> 00:06:44.420
Yes, sir!

00:06:48.920 --> 00:06:49.680
What's wrong?

00:06:50.510 --> 00:06:53.600
Kurau is Dr. Amami's daughter, right?

00:06:55.560 --> 00:06:59.640
You knew that, Inspector. isn't that right?

00:07:16.790 --> 00:07:17.950
Inspector!

00:07:19.330 --> 00:07:20.790
That's something you don't need to know.

00:07:35.970 --> 00:07:37.010
Tastes bad, doesn't it?

00:07:40.140 --> 00:07:41.440
Thanks, Ed!

00:07:42.770 --> 00:07:43.940
He gave me this!

00:07:50.240 --> 00:07:52.240
It's delicious!

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:00.790
The freighter in question has been spotted.

00:08:00.790 --> 00:08:02.460
We'll catch up in fourteen minutes.

00:08:07.880 --> 00:08:08.920
What the...

00:08:08.920 --> 00:08:09.630
What's wrong?

00:08:09.960 --> 00:08:11.470
A ship is approaching.

00:08:11.470 --> 00:08:14.140
Don't tell me... The GPO?

00:08:15.640 --> 00:08:17.970
No... it's different... it's unmarked.

00:08:17.970 --> 00:08:19.390
It's coming right up to us!

00:08:21.680 --> 00:08:23.140
Accelerate and shake it off!

00:08:24.900 --> 00:08:25.940
It's shooting at us!

00:08:51.550 --> 00:08:53.260
Damn pirates...

00:08:56.090 --> 00:08:57.180
Kurau...

00:08:58.100 --> 00:08:59.220
Pirates...

00:09:22.910 --> 00:09:24.210
Open up!

00:09:48.690 --> 00:09:50.310
This is a hold up.

00:09:50.310 --> 00:09:52.440
Everyone calm down and do as I say.

00:09:54.570 --> 00:09:55.530
That's good, guys.

00:09:56.200 --> 00:09:59.240
Next, dump your cargo.

00:09:59.820 --> 00:10:01.950
You've got insurance on it anyway, right?

00:10:03.080 --> 00:10:06.460
Lost your voice? Which one's the captain?!

00:10:10.130 --> 00:10:10.960
A woman?

00:10:12.090 --> 00:10:16.550
All right. I'll release the cargo. Just take it.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:17.510
Oh yeah?

00:10:18.010 --> 00:10:18.840
Get off!

00:10:21.890 --> 00:10:23.850
Get off our ship!

00:10:24.390 --> 00:10:27.480
Man, you've got guts. I like that in a young guy.

00:10:27.480 --> 00:10:28.850
Get away from Kurau!

00:10:29.350 --> 00:10:30.480
Kurau?

00:10:32.060 --> 00:10:33.320
Get away from her NOW!

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:46.950
Doc! Don't do it!

00:10:57.970 --> 00:10:59.590
Ed!

00:11:08.020 --> 00:11:10.730
No!

00:11:20.860 --> 00:11:25.330
Ship number XR-24! Ship number XR-24!

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:28.200
This is the GPO. Respond!

00:11:28.750 --> 00:11:31.170
We know that Kurau is on your ship.

00:11:31.170 --> 00:11:32.960
Kurau, respond!

00:11:37.300 --> 00:11:39.800
So you're a fugitive, too?

00:11:39.800 --> 00:11:41.970
Let's go. We don't have time.

00:11:41.970 --> 00:11:42.970
Damn!

00:11:44.300 --> 00:11:47.720
XR-24 is currently flying idle.

00:11:48.140 --> 00:11:50.890
It will arrive at the rendezvous point in five minutes.

00:11:52.140 --> 00:11:53.940
There's another ship!

00:11:54.270 --> 00:11:55.730
Bring it up on the monitor.

00:11:55.730 --> 00:11:56.480
Yes.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:11:59.530
What on Earth is this?!

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:05.950
XR-24 seems to have sustained some damage.

00:12:05.950 --> 00:12:07.200
Pirates...

00:12:09.330 --> 00:12:10.160
Jose...

00:12:11.500 --> 00:12:13.710
You're going to stow yourself away on their ship?

00:12:14.210 --> 00:12:18.670
I'm sorry... But the GPO must not find us.

00:12:18.670 --> 00:12:21.170
That's okay, Kurau. Go...

00:12:21.670 --> 00:12:22.680
And one more thing...

00:12:23.180 --> 00:12:26.390
There's nothing you need to apologize for.

00:12:38.770 --> 00:12:39.730
Kurau!

00:12:43.650 --> 00:12:46.950
Stay alive. Please.

00:12:48.530 --> 00:12:49.580
Thank you.

00:13:06.550 --> 00:13:08.890
We'll head to the transit station in district Z.

00:13:09.260 --> 00:13:12.600
If we can escape into that port, we should be fine.

00:13:19.360 --> 00:13:24.740
Unit 2 is in pursuit of the pirate ship.
Unit 1 will stay with XR-24.

00:13:25.360 --> 00:13:26.240
Roger.

00:13:26.610 --> 00:13:28.950
Ayaka, the pirate ship is armed.

00:13:29.370 --> 00:13:31.040
I've arranged for backup.

00:13:31.540 --> 00:13:33.370
Keep your distance till they arrive.

00:13:33.370 --> 00:13:33.950
Yes, sir!

00:13:41.550 --> 00:13:43.460
Seems he was killed by a pirate.

00:13:44.090 --> 00:13:47.300
I also don't see the two of them
anywhere aboard the ship.

00:13:47.720 --> 00:13:48.720
I see...

00:13:53.310 --> 00:13:54.730
Jose Rodriguez...

00:13:55.350 --> 00:13:59.400
Rescued by a certain Agent during a freighter accident.

00:14:01.070 --> 00:14:02.940
I believe Kurau was on board.

00:14:03.400 --> 00:14:05.690
With a girl named Christmas.

00:14:06.610 --> 00:14:09.070
Where are the two? Did they get off midway?

00:14:09.530 --> 00:14:10.660
Where are they headed?

00:14:13.580 --> 00:14:17.410
I'm sorry you lost a member of your crew.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.920
There must be an escape pod somewhere...

00:14:24.550 --> 00:14:28.050
When we get closer to Earth, let's use it to escape.

00:14:29.380 --> 00:14:30.390
Christmas...

00:14:31.890 --> 00:14:34.970
Why? Why did Ed...

00:14:36.180 --> 00:14:38.190
Why did Ed die?

00:14:45.900 --> 00:14:47.650
Man, they're persistent.

00:14:47.650 --> 00:14:50.320
The GPO is still after us.

00:14:50.320 --> 00:14:53.830
That's weird. Usually by now, they'd have given up.

00:14:53.830 --> 00:14:55.830
Well, it makes it more interesting, doesn't it?

00:14:55.830 --> 00:14:58.120
They really want us to play with them!

00:14:58.750 --> 00:15:00.920
It's your fault, Doc!

00:15:01.380 --> 00:15:03.960
This wouldn't have happened
if you just did what we always do.

00:15:03.960 --> 00:15:05.880
But no, you had to go kill him...

00:15:09.170 --> 00:15:11.340
You always did annoy me.

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:17.060
I'm so sick of this stale dull world.

00:15:19.480 --> 00:15:21.350
Isn't that right, my friends?!

00:15:21.350 --> 00:15:23.020
Let's have some fun!

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:39.790
Pirates...

00:15:41.620 --> 00:15:44.210
Inspector Wong, a call from Headquarters.

00:15:44.960 --> 00:15:45.880
Headquarters?

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.210
What?! Shoot them down?!

00:15:49.630 --> 00:15:51.300
But then Kurau will...

00:15:51.880 --> 00:15:54.090
We're not concerned with capturing them.

00:15:54.090 --> 00:15:55.470
It's an order from the Commissioner.

00:15:55.470 --> 00:15:57.390
The Commissioner said to kill them?

00:15:57.390 --> 00:15:58.520
I did not say that.

00:15:58.560 --> 00:16:00.180
But in reality...

00:16:00.180 --> 00:16:04.230
Ayaka, all I'm saying is that you have
permission to shoot them down.

00:16:04.900 --> 00:16:07.770
But your first priority should be capturing Kurau.

00:16:08.440 --> 00:16:09.900
Inspector?

00:16:13.320 --> 00:16:17.030
To the unregistered ship ahead, stop immediately!

00:16:17.330 --> 00:16:20.540
If you do not comply, we will be forced to open fire. I repeat...

00:16:20.910 --> 00:16:22.120
Shut up...

00:16:22.620 --> 00:16:24.330
What's the big deal? So I killed one...

00:16:24.330 --> 00:16:25.710
No, two.

00:16:27.880 --> 00:16:29.050
Fire!

00:16:37.930 --> 00:16:41.310
Detective! I'm returning fire! Otherwise...

00:16:41.890 --> 00:16:43.520
Those idiot pirates!

00:16:44.390 --> 00:16:45.650
I give you permission to fire.

00:16:45.650 --> 00:16:46.770
Yes, ma'am!

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:49.780
However, fire only at the Blue unit.

00:16:49.780 --> 00:16:51.690
We're going to stop them from going anywhere!

00:16:51.690 --> 00:16:52.110
Yes, ma'am!

00:17:00.870 --> 00:17:03.410
Yeah, keep 'em coming.

00:17:03.410 --> 00:17:05.170
We'll fire right back at you!

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:05.870
Hey!

00:17:07.460 --> 00:17:09.460
Dammit, don't run!

00:17:17.800 --> 00:17:18.720
There it is.

00:17:29.820 --> 00:17:30.980
Kurau...

00:17:38.910 --> 00:17:42.370
Well, isn't that great? So it was you guys...

00:17:42.370 --> 00:17:44.620
You're the cause of all this trouble.

00:17:45.660 --> 00:17:48.750
Don't I feel like a fool...

00:17:49.420 --> 00:17:52.630
But I gotta thank you for giving me so much fun.

00:17:53.090 --> 00:17:55.880
I really felt alive!

00:17:55.880 --> 00:17:58.510
How dare you?! After what you did to Ed!

00:17:59.010 --> 00:17:59.760
Ed?

00:18:00.300 --> 00:18:01.600
Oh...

00:18:01.600 --> 00:18:02.850
So what?

00:18:03.640 --> 00:18:05.680
People die anyway.

00:18:05.680 --> 00:18:08.770
Sooner or later, they die.

00:18:09.150 --> 00:18:15.320
Think about it. Only fifty years ago,
war ravaged the world.

00:18:15.780 --> 00:18:20.370
Back then, no one thought twice about dying.

00:18:21.160 --> 00:18:24.160
Death was always near us!

00:18:24.160 --> 00:18:25.410
What are you talking about?

00:18:25.410 --> 00:18:29.830
Because death was always near us,
it really made us feel alive!

00:18:30.330 --> 00:18:33.710
I want to feel alive!

00:18:33.710 --> 00:18:35.050
Is that why you killed him?

00:18:35.630 --> 00:18:38.510
That's right! And I'm alive!

00:18:38.800 --> 00:18:42.050
My whole body feels alive with life!

00:18:44.890 --> 00:18:46.850
Do you want to kill me now?

00:18:47.520 --> 00:18:52.400
Try it. This ship's gonna go down soon anyway.

00:18:52.400 --> 00:18:56.610
The stupid GPO shot up the missile pack.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:18:59.780
It'll blow soon and we'll all be dead.

00:18:59.780 --> 00:19:03.280
So until then, let's have some fun!

00:19:06.040 --> 00:19:09.500
Stop talking nonsense and
think of a way to escape.

00:19:09.500 --> 00:19:13.250
Nonsense? So does that mean
you won't fight me to the death?

00:19:13.250 --> 00:19:14.630
Of course not.

00:19:16.340 --> 00:19:17.380
Kurau!

00:19:17.380 --> 00:19:20.840
In that case, I'll make you wanna kill me!

00:19:20.840 --> 00:19:21.840
NO!

00:19:35.230 --> 00:19:36.020
What the...

00:19:36.940 --> 00:19:38.440
Who the hell...

00:19:38.990 --> 00:19:40.450
Who the hell are you?

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:46.910
From a great distance

00:21:39.940 --> 00:21:46.910
Tooku haruka kanata kara

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:56.250
You smile at me

00:21:49.280 --> 00:21:56.250
Kimi ga hohoemu you ni

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:05.420
The hopelessness that lingers from the past

00:21:58.420 --> 00:22:05.420
Kako kara tsuzuku hakanasa

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:14.470
Is depicted in silence

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:14.470
Shizuka ni utsushi dasarete

00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:23.730
Moonlight, please never change

00:22:16.770 --> 00:22:23.730
Moonlight kawarazu ni ite

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:32.830
Moonlight, I'll come to see you

00:22:25.860 --> 00:22:32.830
Moonlight ai ni yuku Kimi ni

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:41.960
Moonlight, I'll come running up and surely

00:22:35.000 --> 00:22:41.960
Moonlight kakenobori kitto

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:51.090
Moonlight, we'll be able to meet again

00:22:44.130 --> 00:22:51.090
Moonlight mou ichido aeru

00:22:53.310 --> 00:23:00.310
Moonlight

00:22:53.310 --> 00:23:00.310
Moonlight

00:23:09.900 --> 00:23:11.870
Next Episode

00:23:10.910 --> 00:23:14.740
She looks just like you
when you first came to our house.

00:23:14.740 --> 00:23:17.160
The only thing that's different
is the length of her hair.

00:23:17.160 --> 00:23:19.540
So, Kurau, tell me...

00:23:19.540 --> 00:23:21.920
Why did you name her Christmas?

00:23:21.920 --> 00:23:24.880
Yesterday, Today, Tomorrow
